WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.975
Open WebUI can support reusable prompts, system prompts, task-specific assistants,

00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:05.913
conversation history, and workspace organization.

00:00:05.913 --> 00:00:10.175
These features help teams turn repeated work into more consistent workflows.

00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:14.050
A reusable prompt can standardize instructions for summarization, drafting, review,

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:15.213
classification, or analysis.

00:00:15.213 --> 00:00:19.863
A task-specific assistant can combine a model choice, instructions, and expected style.

00:00:19.863 --> 00:00:22.963
Prompt templates should be clear, maintainable, and reviewable.

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:27.613
They should explain the task, constraints, output expectations, and any source-handling rules.

00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:31.488
Vague prompts may work once but fail under different inputs.

00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:37.301
Prompts used by a team should be treated as operational artifacts that can be versioned,

00:00:37.301 --> 00:00:38.464
improved, and reviewed.

00:00:38.464 --> 00:00:43.889
Conversation history can improve continuity, but it can also mix contexts in confusing ways.

00:00:43.889 --> 00:00:48.927
A conversation about personal tasks should not become the basis for client work.

00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:52.027
Experimental prompts should not silently shape production workflows.

00:00:52.027 --> 00:00:53.577
Separating personal, client, experimental,

00:00:53.577 --> 00:00:58.227
and production workspaces reduces accidental data mixing and inappropriate reuse of context.

00:00:58.227 --> 00:01:00.164
Good workflow design is practical.

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:03.652
Decide which prompts are reusable, which conversations are disposable,

00:01:03.652 --> 00:01:05.977
which files belong to which collections,

00:01:05.977 --> 00:01:09.465
and which model should be used for which task.

00:01:09.465 --> 00:01:14.502
The goal is to make AI assistance more reliable and less ad hoc.

00:01:14.502 --> 00:01:19.540
A well-organized workspace helps users understand what the assistant is doing and why.
